# hebrew: the Hebrew script and its marks, from Noto Sans Hebrew. A font
# set adds this layer after Noto Sans Mono, which holds no Hebrew, and the
# font draws at Noto Sans Mono's size.
#
# Niqqud, the vowel points, sit mostly under the letters, and the
# cantillation marks of biblical text sit above and below them. The marks
# may use the rows that the set's line spacing adds. Hebrew is room by
# default, and the fit= line says so for the reader.
#
# License: SIL OFL 1.1.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D5: the script layers.
# - ADR-1302 D13: line spacing and fit=.

role=script
source=font:Noto Sans Hebrew
version=3.001
url=https://github.com/notofonts/hebrew/releases/tag/NotoSansHebrew-v3.001
fit=room
